{{!
    @template tool_openapi/local/back_link

    The way back out of a page that was opened from another one. Included as
    a partial so every such page offers the same control in the same place,
    rather than leaving the breadcrumb as the only way back.

    The arrow is decorative on purpose: the label right next to it already
    says where the link goes, so giving the icon its own alternative text
    would make a screen reader announce the destination twice.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * backurl - Where the link goes
    * backlabel - What it says, naming the destination

    Example context (json):
    {
        "backurl": "https://example.com/index.php",
        "backlabel": "Back to access methods"
    }
}}
<div class="mb-3">
    <a href="{{backurl}}" class="btn btn-link pl-0">
        {{#pix}}t/left, core{{/pix}} {{backlabel}}
    </a>
</div>
